WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.996
Caelo BME combines an English desktop workspace with local biomedical analysis tools. This edited walkthrough starts with an actual application screenshot, then presents figures generated by its own analysis engine from the owner provided CLICK S A experiment. It is not a continuous screen recording, and no cloud response is simulated.

00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:40.856
The original Excel workbook contains thirty two physical wells and one hundred recorded cycles per well. All three thousand two hundred prepared measurements were checked against their original cells, signals, and actual timestamps. All thirty two endpoint values also matched. The source file hash stayed unchanged. Raw files are not published.

00:00:40.856 --> 00:01:02.906
The owner supplied eight concentration levels: zero, then ten to the first through ten to the seventh power. Four physical wells correspond to each level. Concentration units and biological independence were not provided. The endpoint is the mean of each well's final five recorded cycles. These assumptions are documented, rather than inferred from a desired trend.

00:01:02.906 --> 00:01:28.276
This is the actual endpoint figure generated by the application analysis engine. Open circles show every physical well. Horizontal lines show means, and error bars show sample standard deviations. All thirty two endpoints are retained. This describes well to well variation; it does not establish biological replication or clinical performance. The displayed response is not forced to increase monotonically.

00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:48.591
The time course uses actual recorded timestamps, rather than the instrument target interval. All three thousand two hundred readings are retained. Lines and shaded bands summarize four physical wells per concentration and cycle. There is no smoothing, interpolation, or removal of points to improve an expected concentration response.

00:01:48.591 --> 00:02:09.402
A closer look separates the four physical wells at the supplied concentration of one thousand. Each line is an individual recorded trace. Isolated jumps can motivate review, but a statistical flag alone does not establish instrument error. No observations are deleted in this walkthrough, and a single trace is not assigned an invented standard deviation.

00:02:09.402 --> 00:02:30.702
The engine also generated local export bundles containing vector figures, statistics, source hashes, and record decisions. Those full bundles remain private because they contain record level data. Public materials include only reviewed derived figures and a method summary. No G P T requests were needed for this local analysis demonstration.

00:02:30.702 --> 00:02:54.487
The wider workspace supports research chat, local paper review, explicit chart mapping, and image folder monitoring. Its interface uses Electron and React, with Python and Matplotlib for fixed local analysis and optional OpenAI Responses for assistance. Source files are read only and outputs are separate. This independent Caelo based research preview is not the official Grok interface.
